---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Radical Process">

  <!-- ── HEADER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <header class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-20 pb-14 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.45em] uppercase text-gray-500 mb-4">Audio Plugins</p>
    <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-7xl font-black tracking-tighter uppercase mb-10 leading-none">
      Radical<br/>Process
    </h1>
    <p class="text-gray-300 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-14">
      Radical Process makes edgy, obsessively detailed audio plugins for artists who refuse to settle
      for the generic, AI-generated sound flooding music today. Built for those who chase their own
      signature tone down to the last decimal, our tools are unapologetically niche and
      unapologetically deep. This is gear for people who care too much—and wouldn't have it any
      other way.
    </p>

  </header>

  <!-- ── PRODUCTS ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">

    <hr class="border-gray-800 mb-16" />

    <section class="mb-24">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mb-1">
          <h2 class="text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">SGD</h2>
          <span class="text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-gray-500 border border-gray-700 px-2 py-1">
            Coming soon
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm tracking-wide uppercase">
          VST3 / AU / Standalone &nbsp;·&nbsp; macOS &amp; Windows
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        SGD — Spatial Gesture Design — turns a sound file into a <em class="not-italic text-white">gesture</em>:
        a sound together with its motion through a virtual room around the listener. You draw the path on the
        room floor, lift it into three dimensions with an elevation curve, bend the timing with a motion curve,
        and bind the result to a MIDI key. Pressing that key does not merely play the sound, it sends it
        travelling — around you, overhead, past your ear.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-10">
        SGD does not pan. It binauralizes every gesture against a physical model of the room, so on headphones
        the sound leaves your head, with distance, air, wall reflections and Doppler all following from the space
        you built. The whole spatial computation runs offline in the background, so playback itself costs almost
        nothing — and every gesture still keeps its own mixer strip with gain, three-band EQ and a send to the
        shared room reverb.
      </p>

      <img src="/img/sgd-edit.png" alt="The SGD edit view: gesture list, trajectory and elevation editors, inspector, and the keyboard along the bottom."
           class="w-full border border-gray-800 mb-12" />

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-6 mb-12">
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Play space like an instrument</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Every gesture lives on a MIDI key, so spatial sound design stops being an automation-lane chore and
            becomes something you perform live, from your DAW or the standalone application.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Sound that leaves your head</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            True binaural rendering, with distance, air absorption and the reflections of your walls. Dial the
            reflections deeper for dense, vivid spaces, and switch the Doppler shift of moving sources on or off
            to taste.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Draw the motion, sculpt the time</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            The waveform is painted along the trajectory, so you see which part of the sample happens where. The
            motion curve then lets the source rush, hesitate, freeze mid-air, or run the path backwards.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Stretch a sound wide open</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Stereo files get a width curve: the two channels spread apart and ride the path like wingtips,
            opening from a point into a wide wash and closing again, drawn as one simple envelope.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Rooms are real, and they are yours</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Width, height and depth in metres, with a wall material of your choice. Resize the room or swap
            concrete for wood and the reflections, the reverb and every gesture adapt automatically. Rooms save
            as self-contained folders, samples included.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium mb-1">Heavy rendering, weightless workflow</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Nothing is ever rendered twice. Reopen a room and it is instantly ready; tweak a curve and only that
            one gesture quietly re-renders while you keep working.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="mb-12">
        <img src="/img/sgd-observe.png" alt="The SGD observe view: the room as a wireframe box, the listener at its centre, and a gesture's path traced in orange."
             class="w-full border border-gray-800" />
        <figcaption class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-3">
          Observe view — a listener at the centre of the room at true scale, every sounding gesture tracing its
          path in its own colour, with a glowing sphere that swells and fades with the loudness of the sound.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/manual/sgd/"
           class="px-5 py-2 border border-gray-600 text-gray-300 text-sm hover:border-white hover:text-white transition-colors">
          Manual
        </a>
        <a href="/manual/sgd/SGD-Manual.pdf"
           class="px-5 py-2 border border-gray-600 text-gray-300 text-sm hover:border-white hover:text-white transition-colors">
          Manual (PDF)
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="border-gray-800 mb-16" />

    <section class="mb-20">
      <div class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-black tracking-tight mb-1">curtis</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm tracking-wide uppercase">VST3 / AU &nbsp;·&nbsp; Intel Mac &amp; Windows</p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-10">
        <a href="https://github.com/RadicalProcess/curtis/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
           class="px-5 py-2 bg-white text-black font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-gray-200 transition-colors">
          Free Download
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/RadicalProcess/curtis"
           class="px-5 py-2 border border-gray-600 text-gray-300 text-sm hover:border-white hover:text-white transition-colors">
          Source Code
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/RadicalProcess/curtis/issues"
           class="px-5 py-2 border border-gray-600 text-gray-300 text-sm hover:border-white hover:text-white transition-colors">
          Bug Report
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.en.html"
           class="px-5 py-2 border border-gray-600 text-gray-300 text-sm hover:border-white hover:text-white transition-colors">
          License (GPL-3)
        </a>
      </div>

    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="border-t border-gray-900 text-center text-gray-600 text-xs py-10 tracking-widest uppercase">
    <p>&copy; 2026 Radical Process. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>

</Layout>

